meta {
  name: Return a copy
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{host}}/loans/{{loanId}}/return
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  200. The loan is kept and moves to Returned, with a returnedAt timestamp beside the
  original dates; the copy goes back on the shelf.

  Both halves are conditional updates. The loan moves only if it is still Active, so two
  concurrent returns cannot both succeed - which would otherwise credit the shelf with two
  copies for one loan. The shelf is credited only if that would not push the available count
  past the total.

  Repeating this is a 409 and the shelf is not credited twice. The audit entry records
  wasOverdue, so the trail carries the fact rather than leaving it to be recomputed from two
  timestamps.
}
